invariant: INV-14
file: webpki_ticket.c
catches: quic_loop_webpki
reason: the configuration hash leaves out the SPKI pins, so a ticket a
  pinned QUIC session received resumes under another pin set, and the
  resumed handshake checks no key against the new pins.
  test/quic_loop_pins.h's resumption rows under another pin set object.

--- old
    hash_len(&s, cfg->spki_pin_count);
    const uint8_t *pin = cfg->spki_pins;
    for (size_t i = 0; i < cfg->spki_pin_count; i++) {
        sha256_update(&s, pin, SHA256_LEN);
        pin += SHA256_LEN;
    }
--- new
    (void)cfg->spki_pins;
